# Metaball — two blurred, alpha-thresholded Skia circles at the screen centre;
# dragging the top circle pulls a gooey blob off the other, and on release it
# springs back to the centre and merges again.
# What this test covers: slow drags up/down/sideways (stretching the blob until
# the circles separate), a long drag towards each screen edge (layer clip grows
# with the circle), a fast fling, re-grabbing the circle while its return spring
# is in flight (new context from the mid-spring position), a rapid series of
# short drags, and taps on/off the circle.
context platform=ios
open "demos://animations/metaball"
wait 2000
wait "label=\"Close\"" 30000
wait 1500
# Slow stretch upwards until the blobs separate, then release (spring home).
gesture pan 201 437 0 -220 1500
wait 1200
# Down, left, right.
gesture pan 201 437 0 250 1200
wait 1200
gesture pan 201 437 -170 0 900
wait 1200
gesture pan 201 437 170 30 900
wait 1200
# Towards the corners / edges.
gesture pan 201 437 -190 -330 1000
wait 1200
gesture pan 201 437 190 380 1000
wait 1200
# Fast fling.
gesture pan 201 437 150 -300 120
wait 1200
# Grab it again while it is springing back.
gesture pan 201 437 0 -300 400
wait 150
gesture pan 201 340 130 -30 500
wait 1200
# Rapid short horizontal drags (a downward drag that misses the circle is the
# app-wide close gesture, so these stay horizontal).
gesture pan 201 437 80 0 150
wait 60
gesture pan 201 437 -80 0 150
wait 60
gesture pan 201 437 80 -40 150
wait 60
gesture pan 201 437 -80 -40 150
wait 1500
# Taps on the circle and on empty canvas.
press 201 437
wait 300
press 60 700
wait 300
press 201 437 --count 4 --interval-ms 80
wait 1000
wait "label=\"Close\"" 15000
press "role=\"button\" label=\"Close\""
wait 1500
